parts.part_stem:
A small coil is placed close to one end of a solenoid connected to a power supply. The plane of the small coil is normal to the axis of the solenoid, as illustrated in Fig. 9.1.
{{figure:9702_w20_42_q09_figure_9_1}}
Fig. 9.1
The power supply causes the current $I$ in the solenoid to vary with time $t$ as shown in Fig. 9.2.
{{figure:9702_w20_42_q09_figure_9_2}}
Fig. 9.2

parts.text:
On the axes of Fig. 9.3, sketch a graph to show the variation with time $t$ of the electromotive force (e.m.f.) induced in the small coil.
{{figure:9702_w20_42_q09_figure_9_3}}
Fig. 9.3
